+# Contract: HTTP API *(delta for `002-burn-and-password-pastes`)*
+
+**Feature**: `002-burn-and-password-pastes` | **Date**: 2026-11-16
+
+This is a **delta** on [the 001 HTTP contract](../../001-pastebin-service/contracts/http-api.md),
+which remains binding in full. Anything not restated here is unchanged: the route table, the base
+address, the common response headers, the error-body shape, the framing rules, and every status
+code and message 001 defines (FR-053).
+
+There is **no new route, no new method, and no new command-line option.** The feature's entire
+caller-facing surface is: two optional request-body fields, one request header, and two fields in
+one response body.
+
+---
+
+## Summary of every change
+
+| Surface | Change | Requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /pastes` body | `burn_after_reading` (optional boolean) accepted | FR-030, FR-031 |
+| `POST /pastes` body | `password` (optional string, 1-128 characters) accepted | FR-032, FR-033 |
+| `POST /pastes` `201` body | **none** — still exactly `{id, delete_token, url}` | FR-035 |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>` request | `X-Paste-Password` header honoured | FR-040 |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>` `200` body | `burn_after_reading` and `protected` added | FR-037 |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` request | `X-Paste-Password` header honoured | FR-040 |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` `200` body/headers | **none** — still the exact content bytes | FR-039 |
+| `DELETE /pastes/<id>` | **none** — token only; a password header is not read | FR-050 |
+| Status codes | `403` is now reachable on both `GET` routes | FR-040 |
+| Error body shape | **none** — still `{"error": "<message>"}` | FR-054 |
+
+---
+
+## Request header: `X-Paste-Password`
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Routes | `GET /pastes/<id>`, `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` only |
+| Required | only when the paste is protected |
+| Value | the password set at creation, as UTF-8 bytes |
+| Encoding | header bytes are interpreted as UTF-8 (the service re-encodes the stdlib's latin-1 decoding and decodes it as UTF-8 — R-19) |
+| Repeated header | the first value is used; access is granted only if that value is the password |
+| Empty value | treated as a wrong password — never a match (a stored password is ≥ 1 character) |
+| Undecodable value | treated as a wrong password |
+| On an unprotected paste | ignored entirely; the read succeeds and the value has no effect (FR-042) |
+| On `DELETE` | not read; has no effect (FR-050) |
+| Echoed in any response | **never** (SR-019) |
+
+---
+
+## `POST /pastes` — create *(delta)*
+
+### New body fields
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Constraints |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `burn_after_reading` | boolean | no | `true` or `false` only. `"true"`, `"false"`, `0`, `1`, `null`, arrays, and objects are rejected. Absent ⇒ `false` |
+| `password` | string | no | 1 … 128 **characters** (not bytes — a 128-character password of multi-byte characters is accepted). Any character a JSON string can hold. `""`, `null`, numbers, booleans, arrays, and objects are rejected. Absent ⇒ unprotected |
+
+Any other field is still ignored (FR-009).
+
+```http
+POST /pastes HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+Content-Type: application/json
+Content-Length: 78
+
+{"content": "recovery code 4821", "burn_after_reading": true, "password": "hunter2"}
+```
+
+### Response `201 Created` — **unchanged**
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ",
+  "delete_token": "9rYQ0s3Xz2mKpLv8wTnB4jHcFdEaGuRi7NsOyPqZlMk",
+  "url": "/pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ"
+}
+```
+
+Exactly three fields, whatever options were used. The response never echoes the password, never
+reports whether the paste is protected, and never reports the one-time marking (FR-035).
+
+### New failure cases
+
+| Condition | Status | Example message |
+|---|---|---|
+| `burn_after_reading` is not a boolean | `400` | `"burn_after_reading must be true or false"` |
+| `password` is not a string | `400` | `"password must be a string of 1 to 128 characters"` |
+| `password` is `""` or longer than 128 characters | `400` | `"password must be a string of 1 to 128 characters"` |
+
+Nothing is created in any of these cases.
+
+### Validation precedence *(FR-036)*
+
+Both new fields are validated **before** the content-size rule:
+
+| Submission | Status |
+|---|---|
+| Invalid new field, content within the limit | `400` |
+| Invalid new field, content **over** the limit | `400` — not `413` |
+| Valid new fields, content over the limit | `413` |
+| Declared `Content-Length` over 66 560 | `413`, body not read *(framing rule, unchanged)* |
+
+---
+
+## `GET /pastes/<id>` — read *(delta)*
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+GET /pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+X-Paste-Password: hunter2
+```
+
+### Response `200 OK` — two fields added
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ",
+  "content": "recovery code 4821",
+  "created_at": "2026-11-16T09:41:07Z",
+  "expires_at": null,
+  "burn_after_reading": true,
+  "protected": true
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `burn_after_reading` | boolean | Present on **every** successful structured read, including pastes that use neither option (FR-037) |
+| `protected` | boolean | Whether a password is required. Reports only *whether* — no response ever contains the password, the stored hash, the salt, or the hashing parameters (FR-038, SR-019) |
+
+`delete_token` is still absent (FR-013). These six fields are the whole body.
+
+### Failure cases *(delta)*
+
+| Condition | Status | Message |
+|---|---|---|
+| Protected, header absent, empty, undecodable, or wrong | `403` | `"invalid paste password"` |
+| Unknown, expired, revoked, or already consumed — **whatever password is supplied** | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| One-time, and a concurrent reader won the claim | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| Protection state cannot be determined (unusable stored record) | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| Claim fails unexpectedly after the password check | `500` | `"internal error"` — no content, no diagnostics (SR-020) |
+
+A `403` body discloses no part of the content, and the paste remains readable to a caller holding
+the password (FR-041).
+
+---
+
+## `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` — read as plain text *(delta)*
+
+Request: identical to the structured read, including `X-Paste-Password`.
+
+Success response: **completely unchanged** — status `200`, `Content-Type: text/plain;
+charset=utf-8`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, body byte-for-byte the content with nothing
+added. Neither flag appears in the body, and no response header carries either flag (FR-039).
+
+Failure responses are the same as the structured read's, and remain JSON-bodied (`{"error": …}`)
+even though the success body is plain text — unchanged from 001.
+
+A successful raw read of a one-time paste consumes it exactly as a structured read does (FR-044).
+
+---
+
+## `DELETE /pastes/<id>` — revoke *(no change)*
+
+Still requires `X-Delete-Token` and nothing else. The password is not required, does not
+substitute for the token, and a password header on this route is not read and has no effect
+(FR-050). A revocation refused with `403` leaves a one-time paste intact and still readable once
+(FR-046). After a one-time paste has been consumed, a revocation with the correct token is `404`
+(FR-045).
+
+---
+
+## Read evaluation order *(normative)*
+
+Both `GET` routes evaluate in exactly this order. Both boundaries are load-bearing.
+
+```text
+1. identifier allowlist + resolved-path containment    → 404
+2. record exists, parses, and is usable                → 404
+3. record is live (not expired)                        → 404
+4. protected ⇒ X-Paste-Password verifies               → 403
+5. one-time ⇒ claim (os.unlink) succeeds               → 404
+6. serve                                               → 200
+```
+
+1. **Steps 1-3 precede step 4** (FR-043): a `403` is only ever returned for an identifier that
+   really resolves to a live paste. An unknown, expired, revoked, or already-consumed identifier
+   is `404` whatever password is supplied, so a refusal never confirms that an identifier is real
+   (SC-016).
+2. **Step 4 precedes step 5** (FR-046): a reader who cannot prove they hold the password never
+   consumes the single read, so a stranger with the link cannot destroy a paste they were never
+   entitled to see.
+3. **Step 6 writes the first byte of content.** Nothing before it discloses any part of the
+   content or its length.
+
+---
+
+## Status codes *(delta)*
+
+| Status | New meaning added by this feature |
+|---|---|
+| `400` | `burn_after_reading` not a boolean; `password` not a 1-128-character string |
+| `403` | **New on `GET` routes**: protected paste read without the correct `X-Paste-Password`. (Unchanged on `DELETE`: wrong or missing `X-Delete-Token`) |
+| `404` | Additionally: already-consumed one-time paste; lost claim race; stored record whose new fields are unusable |
+| `413` | Unchanged — and now explicitly **outranked** by `400` when a new field is invalid (FR-036) |
+| `500` | Additionally: a claim that fails for a reason other than the record already being gone (SR-020) |
+
+**Precedence rules** (001's two, plus one):
+
+1. `413` beats everything for an otherwise-valid oversized submission (FR-027).
+2. `400` beats `413` when a new field is invalid (FR-036) — *new*.
+3. `404` beats `403` everywhere, on reads as well as revocations (FR-043).
+
+---
+
+## What a pre-feature client observes
+
+A client that sends neither new field and no password header sees exactly what it saw before, on
+every route, in every status, header, body shape, error message, and precedence rule — with one
+exception: the structured read now carries `burn_after_reading: false` and `protected: false`
+(FR-053). That is the complete list of observable differences.
